12
00:55:17,142 --> 00:55:23,142
The Bodyguard is a 1992 American romantic thriller drama film directed by Mick Jackson, written by Lawrence Kasdan, and
starring Kevin Costner, Whitney Houston (in her movie acting debut), Gary Kemp, Bill Cobbs, and Ralph Waite.

13
00:59:53,571 --> 00:59:59,571
The film follows a former United States Secret Service agent turned bodyguard who is
hired to protect a famous actor and singer from an unknown stalker.

14
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
Kasdan wrote the film in the mid-1970s, originally
as a vehicle for Steve McQueen.

15
01:09:06,428 --> 01:09:12,428
The Bodyguard was theatrically released by Warner Bros.

16
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:48,857
Pictures on November 25, 1992.

17
01:18:19,285 --> 01:18:25,285
The film grossed $411 million worldwide, becoming the second-highest-grossing
film of 1992, but received mostly unfavorable reviews from critics.

18
01:22:55,714 --> 01:23:01,714
The film's accompanying soundtrack by Houston became the best-selling soundtrack album of all time, with
sales of over 45 million copies worldwide, and won the Grammy Award for Album of the Year.

19
01:27:32,142 --> 01:27:38,142
The lead single "I Will Always Love You" achieved unprecedented worldwide success, selling over 24 million copies worldwide, and is
still the best-selling single in history by a woman as well as the best-selling single by a female artist of all time.

20
01:32:08,571 --> 01:32:14,571
The other singles "I Have Nothing" and "Run to You" received
nominations for the Academy Award for Best Original Song.

21
01:36:45,000 --> 01:36:51,000
The film received seven nominations at the 13th Golden Raspberry Awards, including for
Worst Picture, Worst Actor (for Costner) and Worst Actress (for Houston).

22
01:41:21,428 --> 01:41:27,428
In spite of the Razzies, Houston received best acting nominations at the People's
Choice Awards, MTV Movie & TV Awards and the NAACP Image Awards.

23
01:45:57,857 --> 01:46:03,857
Billboard later listed Houston's performance in the film as the 27th
best performance of a musician in a box-office film.

24
01:50:34,285 --> 01:50:40,285
It has been reevaluated from critics and has
developed a cult following over time.

25
01:55:10,714 --> 01:55:16,714
The film and soundtrack cemented Houston's status as a pop culture icon.

26
01:59:47,142 --> 01:59:53,142
The film explores themes of sibling relationship,
bodyguard, anonymous letter, diva, stalker.

27
02:04:23,571 --> 02:04:29,571
The tone is emotional.
